California is aiming to put a stop to  the often inhumane conditions of puppy  mills it's now the first state in the  nation to require pet stores to sell  rescue animals Artur Evans has the story  the Humane Society estimates more than  two million dogs sold in the u.s. each  year come from so-called puppy mills  like this one in Florida this unlicensed  breeding operation has overcrowded and  unsanitary conditions many dogs had no  access to clean drinking water and were  suffering from various medical  conditions the only way to shut this  cruel industry down is to take away the  demand animal advocate Judi Mancuso  helped pass the new California law which  requires pet stores to only sell dogs  cats and rabbits that are rescues in the  state of California we bring in over  800,000 dogs and cats into our shelters  and we kill over half why on earth are  we allowing this cruel industry to be  feeding our state with yet more animals  but the new law will still allow  Californians to buy animals directly  from reputable breeders Boris Jiang  sells pure brands along with rescues in  his Sante in a pet store if it was only  shelter dogs would you still be in  business no to sell the puppies that  allows us to do the adoptions the  reality is it takes the sale of a $1,500  dog to help fund the sale of a shelter  dog absolutely James says the new law  will likely force his business to close  but Andrew Kim who runs the pet store  chain healthy spot has a different  business approach the only animals here  are rescues we've saved over 500 dogs  and cats and hopefully we've built some  customers along the way as well Kim  believes it's not only the humane choice  but a savvy one where does the bulk of  your income come from if it doesn't come  from the animal sales  it's the supplies and services healthy  spot offers everything from treats and  toys to grooming services and his  business is growing Kim now owns 11  stores around the state when you  open your home in heart to loving animal  right like this dog here why wouldn't  you want to support the store where you  made that first connection how could you  resist faces like this right  the puppies hope you can't for CBS this  morning Saturday Carter Evans Los  Angeles  they are prettier I we adopted a rescue  and rooster is a blessing every day  no I encourage everyone to do it great  advice
 

